#
# Bug#39254885 - reject DECIMAL user var metadata that overruns the payload
#
# R2: payload matches the declared precision and scale, so it decodes.
include/assert_grep.inc [a well-formed DECIMAL user var event is not rejected]
# R1: declared precision 65 over a two-byte payload needs 29 bytes, so the
#     event must be refused instead of read past its end.
include/assert_grep.inc [the oversized DECIMAL metadata is rejected while decoding]
